On Fri, May 7, 2010 at 11:29 AM, tijlan <jbotijlan@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> For "fifty or sixty people" (meaning "between fifty and sixty people"), I
> would like to use "bi'i", but I'm not sure whether {muno bi'i xano prenu}
> would be valid.

No, you need "vei muno bi'i xano (ve'o) prenu".

I prefer "su'o muno su'e xano prenu", if fifty/sixty are included,
"za'u muno me'i xano prenu", if they are not, "(ji'i) muno ji'i xano
prenu" if it's an approximate range.

> {li muno bi'i xano} seems valid as a mex though.

Yes.

